      "content": "Tech companies often rebut the Right to Repair with several arguments. They claim security concerns are paramount; unauthorized repairs might lead to security vulnerabilities being exploited. They also stress the necessity of standardized parts and repair processes to ensure products function and remain reliable. Another argument is the protection of intellectual property and brand value, with companies arguing that DIY repairs could lead to counterfeiting and brand dilution. Lastly, these companies tout their direct repair services, prioritizing customer safety and a full warranty during factory-approved repairs as superior to third-party repair attempts.",
